WEBVTT

NOTE Unofficial English translation of the Thai narration. If it differs from the Thai original documents, the Thai original prevails.

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:07.731
The Subcommittee on Water Management in
Agricultural Areas Outside Irrigation

00:00:07.731 --> 00:00:13.759
Zones has scheduled Meeting No. 21/2569
for Tuesday, 24 November 2026.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:20.860
At 2 p.m., in committee room CA
320, 3rd floor, Parliament House.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.780
The subcommittee chair
is Miss Amorn Sribunnak.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:29.614
This subcommittee is part
of the Senate Committee

00:00:29.614 --> 00:00:32.118
on Agriculture and Cooperatives.

00:00:32.199 --> 00:00:36.160
The committee chair is
Mr. Sountorn Chaokijka.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:41.440
The committee's three current
subcommittees are chaired as follows.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.100
Livestock and Fisheries:
Mr. Ruchu Kaewlai.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:51.440
Water Management in Farm Areas Outside
Irrigation Zones: Miss Amorn Sribunnak.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:55.860
And Integrated Agricultural
Networks: Mr. Choocheep Auekarn.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:00.357
This meeting was scheduled
by a resolution of

00:01:00.357 --> 00:01:03.698
the subcommittee on
Wednesday, 18 November.

00:01:03.779 --> 00:01:08.329
The agenda has three items:
announcements from the chair,

00:01:08.329 --> 00:01:12.719
adoption of the minutes, and
matters for consideration.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:17.471
Under matters for consideration,
the meeting will consider the draft

00:01:17.471 --> 00:01:21.867
study report on guidelines for
efficient, secure and sustainable

00:01:21.867 --> 00:01:26.263
water management in agricultural
areas outside irrigation zones.

00:01:26.345 --> 00:01:30.000
This is the complete version,
to be submitted to the Senate.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.730
Earlier, at Meeting No. 39 of
the Committee on Agriculture

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.666
and Cooperatives on 16 November, the

00:01:38.666 --> 00:01:42.499
subcommittee chair presented
this draft report.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:46.198
The draft proposes a
three-phase approach:

00:01:46.198 --> 00:01:49.126
urgent, medium-term and long-term.

00:01:49.207 --> 00:01:56.400
The committee asked all members to
review the report in detail once more.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:59.340
If no member requests
changes, the meeting

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:02.200
will be deemed to have
approved the draft.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.000
This preview is based on the
subcommittee's meeting notice.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.995
Meeting results are available
through the channels

00:02:09.995 --> 00:02:11.919
of the Secretariat of the Senate.

